{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 38, :comments ["<b>who eat the fat of their sacrifices</b> — for Israel were constant in the service of sacrifices and libations more than any nation to its elohim. And he used plural language: 'their elohim shall eat and drink' (referring to אֱלֹהֵימוֹ, 'their elohim,' which is plural in form), for among the nations they are many, and therefore he went back and said, 'See now that I, I am He' (Deuteronomy 32:39) — I am unique, and there is no elohim with Me to help Me, and there is none against Me to deliver and to stay My hand from doing all My will — to kill and to wound, to give life and to heal."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:15:46.972288682Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}